{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: `_refresh` has no guard against a throwing runner**

```dart
Future<void> _refresh(String cwd) async {
  final output = await _run(cwd);   // ← throws → unhandled async error
  …
}
```

`_refresh` is launched via `unawaited(...)` from `current()`, so if the injected `GitStatusRunner` throws, the error surfaces as an unhandled async exception (zone crash in tests, stack-noise in production). The default `_runGitStatus` catches `on Object`, so only custom runners can trigger this — but `GitStatusRunner` is a public typedef and nothing documents a no-throw contract.

Either wrap the body:

```dart
Future<void> _refresh(String cwd) async {
  final String? output;
  try {
    output = await _run(cwd);
  } on Object {
    output = null;
  }
  …
}
```

…or add one line to the `GitStatusRunner` doc: *"Must not throw — return null to signal failure."* The first option is safer; the injectable seam exists precisely so tests can substitute runners freely.
